\f0\fs28 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 These results present a mixed and potentially productive leadership profile: comparatively strong humility, empathy, and ethical intent sit alongside elevated scores related to strategic guardedness, emotional detachment, and comfort with hard-edged decisions. The most useful interpretation is not \'93what kind of person am I?\'94 but \'93under which conditions might particular behaviours become more or less likely?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Important limitation:
\f0\b0  This is a developmental interpretation, not a psychological diagnosis or fitness-for-leadership judgment. Scores cannot be classified reliably as low, moderate, or high without knowing the questionnaire, its comparison group, validity, and scoring norms. Even clinical assessment measures should not be used alone to make diagnoses, and a workplace self-report carries additional limitations such as current mood, interpretation of questions, and self-presentation. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.psychiatry.org/File%20Library/Psychiatrists/Practice/DSM/APA_DSM5_The-Personality-Inventory-For-DSM-5-Full-Version-Adult.pdf"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [psychiatry.org]}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.apa.org/about/policy/guidelines-psychological-assessment-evaluation.pdf"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [apa.org]}}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 1. Balanced interpretation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Overall pattern\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Your profile may describe a leader who:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Can make difficult decisions without becoming overwhelmed by emotion.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Thinks strategically about incentives, interests, influence, and organisational politics.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sees ethical conduct and personal humility as important.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Has meaningful capacity to understand other people\'92s perspectives.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 May nevertheless become more instrumental, emotionally distant, or outcome-focused under pressure.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The central developmental question is whether your 
\f1\b empathy, humility, and ethical standards remain active when the stakes rise
\f0\b0 , rather than only when conditions are calm.\
Research connects elevated \'93dark trait\'94 measures with workplace risks on average, but these are probabilistic relationships, not predictions about an individual. Authority, organisational culture, regulation, justice perceptions, and other contextual conditions can substantially affect how traits are expressed. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/psychology/articles/10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1738277/full"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [frontiersin.org]}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11939815/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov]}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Donelson-Forsyth/publication/309076033_A_meta-analysis_of_the_dark_triad_and_work_outcomes_A_social_exchange_perspective/links/580e7f4608ae47535247b61d/A-meta-analysis-of-the-dark-triad-and-work-outcomes-A-social-exchange-perspective.pdf"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [researchgate.net]}}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 What each score might contribute\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa372\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Narcissism: 46/100\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 Without norms, this appears closer to the middle of the scale than to an extreme. It may suggest:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Some confidence, ambition, or desire to have visible impact.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A manageable rather than dominating need for recognition.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Possible sensitivity when expertise, status, or competence is publicly challenged.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Potential leadership expression:
\f0\b0  You may be comfortable taking ownership while still being able to share the stage. Under identity threat, however, you may become more defensive, argumentative, or concerned with controlling the narrative.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa372\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Machiavellianism: 64/100\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 This may signal a relatively strong strategic and politically aware orientation:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You may notice hidden interests, power relationships, and incentive structures quickly.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You may be comfortable negotiating, withholding premature commitments, and planning several moves ahead.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You may place more weight on demonstrated behaviour than on stated intentions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Potential leadership expression:
\f0\b0  This can support stakeholder navigation and negotiation. The risk appears when strategic thinking becomes excessive information control, covert influence, testing loyalty, or treating relationships mainly as means to an end.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa372\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Psychopathy: 68/100\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 In a non-clinical workplace questionnaire, this label often samples qualities such as fearlessness, low emotional reactivity, impulsivity, or reduced sensitivity to others\'92 distress. It does 
\f1\b not
\f0\b0  establish clinical psychopathy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Potential leadership expression:
\f0\b0  You may remain composed in emergencies, tolerate conflict, and make unpopular decisions. Under fatigue, competition, or time pressure, the same pattern could appear as impatience, insufficient concern about emotional consequences, excessive bluntness, or rapid risk-taking.\
Workplace research finds average associations between higher scores on such measures and counterproductive behaviour, but performance relationships are not simple, and context can substantially moderate outcomes. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11939815/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov]}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Donelson-Forsyth/publication/309076033_A_meta-analysis_of_the_dark_triad_and_work_outcomes_A_social_exchange_perspective/links/580e7f4608ae47535247b61d/A-meta-analysis-of-the-dark-triad-and-work-outcomes-A-social-exchange-perspective.pdf"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [researchgate.net]}}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa372\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Sadism: 43/100\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 This score does not appear elevated on its face, although norms are still required. It may indicate that deriving satisfaction from another person\'92s discomfort is not a prominent self-reported tendency.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Potential leadership expression:
\f0\b0  This may reduce concern about intentionally humiliating or punishing people. It does not eliminate the possibility that bluntness, humour, public challenge, or harsh accountability could be experienced as harmful even when causing discomfort was not your intention.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa372\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Empathy: 61/100\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 This suggests a useful capacity for perspective-taking or emotional awareness.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Potential leadership expression:
\f0\b0  You may be able to anticipate reactions and understand competing viewpoints. Empathy is most protective when it changes your behaviour. Accurately reading someone without giving their interests ethical weight can otherwise become merely a tool for persuasion.\
Empathic leadership conversations can help people feel invited, cared for, and valued, particularly when leaders use feeling-based questions and create space for two-way meaning-making. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11301-024-00472-7"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [link.springer.com]}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/business-ethics-quarterly/article/abs/role-of-empathy-in-leadership-ethics-examining-empathic-relational-leadership-practice-through-videobased-methods/306215B36DE1325557D459BE781001C9"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [cambridge.org]}}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa372\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Humility: 75/100\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 This is one of the strongest apparent protective signals in the profile. It may reflect willingness to:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Recognise limitations.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Learn from other people.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Admit mistakes.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Give credit.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Revise a position in response to evidence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Expressed humility has been associated with information sharing, mentoring, psychological safety, shared leadership, and related positive outcomes. The important word is 
\f1\b expressed
\f0\b0 : colleagues must be able to observe it in decisions and interactions. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/psychology/articles/10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1839157/full"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [frontiersin.org]}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10551-023-05523-9"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [link.springer.com]}}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa372\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Ethical Leadership: 68/100\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 This suggests that fairness, responsible conduct, and moral standards are meaningful parts of your leadership self-concept.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Potential leadership expression:
\f0\b0  You may be motivated to set boundaries, uphold standards, and consider broader consequences. The risk is ethical overconfidence, especially when a leader assumes that good intentions make additional scrutiny unnecessary. Your ethical orientation becomes more protective when supported by transparent criteria, consultation, documentation, and permission for others to challenge you.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Likely leadership style\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 A concise working hypothesis would be:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 A strategically minded, relatively fearless and decisive leader with meaningful ethical and interpersonal safeguards, whose main risk arises when urgency, competition, or threat causes strategy and emotional detachment to outrun consultation and care.
\f0\b0 \
This could be effective in transformation, crisis response, negotiation, turnaround work, or politically complex environments. It may be less effective when success depends on slow trust-building, psychological safety, developmental coaching, or consultation with people who have less power.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Possible biases\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Watch particularly for:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Outcome bias:
\f0\b0  Deciding that a process was acceptable because the result was favourable.\
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Control bias:
\f0\b0  Assuming centrally controlled information will produce better decisions.\
\ls5\ilvl0
