\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 5. Short workplace scripts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Seeking feedback\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93I am working on how I make decisions under pressure. What is one observable behaviour I should continue, and one I should adjust? I am looking for a concrete example, not a personality judgment.\'94\
Alternative:\
\'93When I am moving quickly, do I still make enough room for challenge? Please tell me about a recent occasion when I did or did not.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Pausing before a reactive decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93I am aware that I am reacting strongly. Unless there is an immediate safety or operational need, I am going to pause, review the facts and consequences, and return to this tomorrow.\'94\
Short version:\
\'93This matters, and I do not want urgency to reduce judgment quality. Let me come back with a considered decision.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Giving credit\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93The key contribution here came from [name/team]. They identified [specific issue or opportunity], which enabled [specific result]. I want that contribution to be visible.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Repairing harm\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93My approach in that conversation had a negative impact. I interrupted you and closed down discussion before fully hearing your concern. That was not appropriate. I am sorry. Next time I will hear the evidence first and summarise it before responding. Is there anything practical I should do now to repair the situation?\'94\
Avoid adding \'93but,\'94 explaining away the impact, or asking the affected person to reassure you.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Responding ethically to conflict\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93Let us separate the facts, interests, impact, and decision criteria. I want each person to be heard, and I will not use disagreement itself as evidence of disloyalty.\'94\
For a power-imbalanced conflict:\
\'93I recognise that my role affects how safe it feels to disagree with me. You may raise concerns directly, in writing, or through the appropriate independent channel. Respectful challenge will not be penalised.\'94\
For an integrity concern:\
\'93I will not trade policy, fairness, or another person\'92s dignity for a faster result. Let us identify an option that meets the objective within those boundaries.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

