\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 7. Final perspective\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Treat these results as 
\f1\b hypotheses to test against observable behaviour
\f0\b0 , not as labels or forecasts. A moderately or highly elevated score does not mean that harmful conduct will occur, while reassuring scores do not guarantee ethical behaviour. Self-report results should be integrated with context, validated norms, behavioural examples, structured feedback, and, where warranted, interpretation by a qualified professional. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.psychiatry.org/File%20Library/Psychiatrists/Practice/DSM/APA_DSM5_The-Personality-Inventory-For-DSM-5-Full-Version-Adult.pdf"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [psychiatry.org]}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.apa.org/about/policy/guidelines-psychological-assessment-evaluation.pdf"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [apa.org]}}\
Your most promising development strategy is not to suppress decisiveness or strategic thinking. It is to place those capacities inside visible safeguards: consultation, transparent criteria, proportionality, independent challenge, respectful communication, and repair when impact falls short of intent. Protect colleagues\'92 privacy and dignity throughout. Do not assess, label, or speculate about other people using these constructs, and do not share anyone\'92s feedback or psychological information without a legitimate purpose and appropriate consent.\
}